A1 L2: pocket grid: a person on a sheer D 3 (1.5 m) pit floor is held and cannot walk out, a muffalo beside it is free, a rat in a sheer D 2 is trapped, a person in the dried-pond D 2 ring / D 4 core walks out, and filling a wall re-frees the pit (climb_proof rows CLIMB_pond_*, CLIMB_D3_*, CLIMB_D2_rat_trapped, CLIMB_rebuild_follows_fill all PASS).
A2 L2: cliff masks: the person band's A* has no step down a 2 m wall the muffalo band has, a step of exactly K is priced slow, a ramp lets a person walk out and removing it re-traps, a lowered ladder frees our colonist and not a wild rat, a raider on a ramp-less island in a sheer moat cannot reach the map edge (CLIMB_mask_seals_cliff_edge, CLIMB_step_cost_slow_at_K, CLIMB_ramp_*, CLIMB_ladder_prison_door, CLIMB_raider_never_crosses_ramped_moat all PASS).
A3 L2: the per-request mask swap holds under 1.6's multithreaded pathfinding while masks rebuild: a churn dig re-derives the masks every 6 ticks (>= 20 FullDerives) while >= 30 drafted orders queue path requests; two surface colonists walk round a sheer D 4 pit (>= 2 side changes) and the colonist on its floor never leaves it; no pawn is ever sampled across the wall (CLIMB_maskswap_no_wall_crossing PASS).
A4 L2: a direct raid against an island ringed by a sheer 2 m trench: the island reads sealed (RAID_island_sealed PASS) and what the raiders did (BREACH / FELL / LEFT / STALL / MILL / SHOT_ACROSS) is recorded in RAID_outcome (MEASURED with an outcome).
